      "rust_file": "src/search_command.rs",
      "rust_item": "fn[find_matches]",
      "text": [
        "/// Collect matches from the loaded registry and from every package manager.",
        "pub async fn find_matches(sym: &Symposium, query: &str) -> Vec<SearchMatch> {",
        "    let mut matches = Vec::new();",
        "",
        "    let registry = crate::plugins::load_registry(sym).await;",
        "    // Plugins already listed, by (registry, plugin name). A registry's search",
        "    // hit names an entry directory, which can differ from the plugin's name.",
        "    let mut listed = std::collections::HashSet::new();",
        "    for parsed in &registry.plugins {",
        "        if name_matches(&parsed.manifest.name, query) {",
        "            listed.insert((parsed.canonical.pm.clone(), parsed.canonical.name.clone()));",
        "            matches.push(SearchMatch {",
        "                origin: parsed.canonical.pm.clone(),",
        "                name: parsed.manifest.name.clone(),",
        "                version: None,",
        "                description: parsed",
        "                    .manifest",
        "                    .requires_use",
        "                    .then(|| \"dormant — enable with `cargo agents use`\".to_string()),",
        "            });",
        "        }",
        "    }",
        "    // Search is workspace-independent; a detached resolver stands in.",
        "    let pms = sym.detached_managers();",
        "    for (instance, info) in pms.search(query).await {",
        "        if matches",
        "            .iter()",
        "            .any(|m| m.origin == instance && m.name == info.id.name)",
        "        {",
        "            continue;",
        "        }",
        "        // A hit from a registry that already supplied a listed plugin may be",
        "        // that plugin's entry under its directory name. Loading the entry is a",
        "        // local read; other instances' hits are never loaded here.",
        "        if listed.iter().any(|(pm, _)| *pm == instance) {",
        "            let entry = pms.load_plugin(&info.id, UpdateLevel::None).await;",
        "            if entry",
        "                .iter()",
        "                .any(|p| listed.contains(&(p.canonical.pm.clone(), p.canonical.name.clone())))",
        "            {",
        "                continue;",
        "            }",
        "        }",
        "        matches.push(SearchMatch {",
        "            origin: instance,",
        "            name: info.id.name.clone(),",
        "            version: Some(info.id.version.clone()),",
        "            description: info.description,",
        "        });",
        "    }",
        "",
        "    matches",
        "}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "rust_file": "src/search_command.rs",
      "rust_item": "fn[search]",
      "text": [
        "/// The `cargo agents search` entry point: report every match grouped by the",
        "/// instance it came from, or a nothing-found message.",
        "pub async fn search(sym: &Symposium, query: &str) -> Result<()> {",
        "    let matches = find_matches(sym, query).await;",
        "    if matches.is_empty() {",
        "        tracing::info!(",
        "            report = %ReportEvent::Info {",
        "                message: format!(\"no plugins matching `{query}` found\"),",
        "            },",
        "        );",
        "        return Ok(());",
        "    }",
        "",
        "    // Group by origin, preserving the order origins were first seen (loaded",
        "    // registry first, then package managers in config order).",
        "    let mut origins: Vec<&str> = Vec::new();",
        "    for m in &matches {",
        "        if !origins.contains(&m.origin.as_str()) {",
        "            origins.push(&m.origin);",
        "        }",
        "    }",
        "    for origin in origins {",
        "        tracing::info!(",
        "            report = %ReportEvent::Info { message: format!(\"from {origin}:\") },",
        "        );",
        "        for m in matches.iter().filter(|m| m.origin == origin) {",
        "            tracing::info!(",
        "                report = %ReportEvent::SearchMatch {",
        "                    origin: m.origin.clone(),",
        "                    name: m.name.clone(),",
        "                    version: m.version.clone(),",
        "                    description: m.description.clone(),",
        "                },",
        "            );",
        "        }",
        "    }",
        "    Ok(())",
        "}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "rust_file": "src/pm/mod.rs",
      "rust_item": "impl[PmRegistry]/fn[search]",
      "text": [
        "    /// Search every instance for packages matching `query`, tagged with the",
        "    /// instance's display name. A failing instance is skipped with a debug log",
        "    /// rather than failing the union.",
        "    pub async fn search(&self, query: &str) -> Vec<(String, PluginInfo)> {",
        "        let mut out = Vec::new();",
        "        for inst in self.instances() {",
        "            match inst.pm.search(query).await {",
        "                Ok(infos) => out.extend(infos.into_iter().map(|info| (inst.name.clone(), info))),",
        "                Err(e) => {",
        "                    tracing::debug!(instance = %inst.name, error = %e, \"search failed, skipping\");",
        "                }",
        "            }",
        "        }",
        "        out",
        "    }"
      ]
    },
    {
      "rust_file": "src/plugins.rs",
      "rust_item": "fn[entry_plugin]",
      "text": [
        "/// The unvalidated plugin for a registry entry at `root/subpath`: a `Symposium.toml`",
        "/// manifest read as-is, or a bare `SKILL.md` synthesized into one",
        "/// ([`standalone_skill_manifest`]). `None` when the directory is neither.",
        "/// Called by [`PathPm`](crate::pm::PathPm).",
        "///",
        "/// Skill paths are displayed relative to the registry root, so an entry reads",
        "/// as `path:<entry>/skills` rather than `path:skills`.",
        "pub(crate) fn entry_plugin(",
        "    root: &Path,",
        "    subpath: &Path,",
        "    source_name: &str,",
        ") -> Option<Result<UnvalidatedPlugin>> {",
        "    let dir = root.join(subpath);",
        "    Some(match crate::pm::layout::classify(&dir)? {",
        "        crate::pm::layout::EntryKind::Plugin(toml_path) => (|| -> Result<UnvalidatedPlugin> {",
        "            let content = fs::read_to_string(&toml_path)?;",
        "            let manifest = RawPluginManifest::parse(&content)?;",
        "            let base = toml_path.parent().unwrap_or(&dir).to_path_buf();",
        "            let name = manifest.name.clone().unwrap_or_default();",
        "            Ok(UnvalidatedPlugin::new(",
        "                PackageId::new(source_name, name, ANY_VERSION),",
        "                base,",
        "                manifest,",
        "            )",
        "            .with_label_root(root))",
        "        })()",
        "        .with_context(|| format!(\"loading plugin from `{}`\", toml_path.display())),",
        "        crate::pm::layout::EntryKind::Skill(skill_md) => (|| -> Result<UnvalidatedPlugin> {",
        "            let manifest = standalone_skill_manifest(&skill_md)?;",
        "            let base = skill_md.parent().unwrap_or(&dir).to_path_buf();",
        "            let name = manifest.name.clone().unwrap_or_default();",
        "            Ok(UnvalidatedPlugin::new(",
        "                PackageId::new(source_name, name, ANY_VERSION),",
        "                base,",
        "                manifest,",
        "            )",
        "            .with_label_root(root))",
        "        })()",
        "        .with_context(|| format!(\"loading skill from `{}`\", skill_md.display())),",
        "    })",
        "}"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "`cargo agents search <query>` dispatches to `search_command::search` (`cli.rs`, `Commands::Search`), which takes every hit from `find_matches`. Each `SearchMatch` has a required `origin` field, and both ways a hit is built set it:\n\n- **Loaded registry plugins** (first arm): `origin = parsed.canonical.pm`. `load_registry` loads only the trusted registry instances. `validate_plugin` sets `canonical` to the id that the package manager returned. That id comes from `entry_plugin`, which builds it as `PackageId::new(source_name, …)` for both a `Symposium.toml` entry and a bare `SKILL.md`. Here `source_name` is the `PathPm`'s name. A `GitPm` passes its configured registry name to its inner `PathPm`. So the tag is always the name of the configured registry the plugin was loaded from (`user-plugins`, `symposium-recommendations`, …).\n- **Package-manager hits** (second arm): `PmRegistry::search` pairs every `PluginInfo` with `inst.name`, and that name becomes `origin`. A registry instance's name is its configured name. The cargo transport is named `cargo` (`CARGO_PM`), and its search queries crates.io, so a crates.io hit is tagged `cargo`, which is the transport that searched crates.io. A failing instance contributes no hits, so no hit is left untagged.\n- The dedup steps (same origin and name, or a registry hit whose entry loads as an already listed plugin of the same registry) only drop duplicates of hits that are already tagged. They never create an untagged hit.\n\nRendering: `search` groups the matches by origin and prints a `from <origin>:` heading before each group. Each hit is emitted as a `ReportEvent::SearchMatch` that carries `origin`, so `--json` output has it on every hit. The human form leaves out the per-line origin because the heading already shows it.\n\nTests (all pass, re-run now):\n- `search_finds_registry_content_tagged_by_origin` asserts that a registry entry has `origin == \"user-plugins\"`.\n- `search_renders_grouped_by_origin` asserts the heading `info` event and a `search_match` event with `origin == \"user-plugins\"`.\n- `status_reports_dormant_registry_plugin` asserts that a dormant manifest plugin found by search has `origin == \"user-plugins\"`.\n\nLimits: no test covers the origin of a crates.io (`cargo`) hit or of a git-registry hit. Those cases are judged from code: `PmRegistry::search` tags them with the instance name, and `GitPm::new` gives its inner `PathPm` the registry name. A crates.io hit is tagged with the transport name `cargo`, not the literal string `crates.io`. That still names its source unambiguously, since `CargoPm::search` only queries crates.io.",
  "requirement": "`cargo agents search <query>` MUST tag each hit with the registry it comes from."
}
